Charlotte recorded the height $H$ (metres) of a tree at various years $t$ since planting:

\begin{array}{c|cccccccc} t\ (\text{years}) & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 \\ \hline H\ (\text{m}) & 0.7 & 1.4 & 2.4 & 3.5 & 6.6 & 7.9 & 8.7 & 9.5 \end{array}

What is the correlation coefficient for this data (correct to 4 decimal places)?

Charlotte's tree height data is shown below.

\begin{array}{c|cccccccc} t\ (\text{years}) & 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 6 & 7 & 8 & 9 \\ \hline H\ (\text{m}) & 0.7 & 1.4 & 2.4 & 3.5 & 6.6 & 7.9 & 8.7 & 9.5 \end{array}

Find the equation of the least-squares line of best fit, where $H = A + Bt$. Give $A$ and $B$ correct to 2 decimal places.
